firmware: qcom: uefisecapp: hand over from the generic efivars operations

The firmware of some machines still answers the EFI runtime variable
services, so the generic operations are registered at boot, but keeps what
is written there in RAM only. efivars_register() of this driver then returns
-EBUSY and the variables stay volatile.

Unregister the generic operations before registering the app's, as the
StMM driver does, and register them again when the app's registration fails
or the client is removed. On machines without the generic operations both
calls do nothing.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom_uefisecapp.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom_uefisecapp.c
@@ -829,9 +829,19 @@
 	if (status)
 		return status;
 
+	/*
+	 * Some firmware still answers the EFI runtime variable services but keeps
+	 * what is written there in RAM only, and the generic operations are then
+	 * registered already, so efivars_register() would return -EBUSY. Hand over
+	 * to the app, which has the persistent store, and go back if that fails.
+	 */
+	efivars_generic_ops_unregister();
+
 	status = efivars_register(&qcuefi->efivars, &qcom_efivar_ops);
-	if (status)
+	if (status) {
+		efivars_generic_ops_register();
 		qcuefi_set_reference(NULL);
+	}
 
 	return status;
 }
@@ -841,6 +851,7 @@
 	struct qcuefi_client *qcuefi = auxiliary_get_drvdata(aux_dev);
 
 	efivars_unregister(&qcuefi->efivars);
+	efivars_generic_ops_register();
 	qcuefi_set_reference(NULL);
 }
 
